Throughout my career in docs, I've wrestled with trying to find the root of how we make our docs better. I've talked before about how the solution to docs isn't always more docs. And as the breadth of KB management grows, I'm increasingly thinking the solution to docs may be less. I've valued efficiency of language in documentation from the beginning, but I rarely thought about the economics of scale. 

## Google and the Scott Towel effect

When I was young, my grandmother would ask me for paper towels by saying "Hand me a Scott towel." You've probably heard someone ask you for a "Kleenex". 

The point I'm making is that it's easy to conflate your KB's search with Google search, even when you know you're working with a specific vendor or tool for this component. 